From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 11:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] panfrost: add the Mali-G710 model row biblioklept

A Pixel 7 (Tensor G2) reports gpu_id 0xa8620004 and panvk drops it with
"Unknown gpu_id (0xa8620004) or variant (0)". 0xa862 is kbase TODX
(GPU_ID2_MODEL_MAKE(10, 2), "Mali-G710"): the same Valhall v10 core as
the G610 (LODX, 0xa867), in 7-16 core configurations. Reuse the G610
tile buffer sizes and rates, which describe one core.

G510 (TGRX, product major 3) is not added: its arch minor is unseen
and pan_model matches the full (major, minor, product) id.

---
 src/panfrost/model/pan_model.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/model/pan_model.c b/src/panfrost/model/pan_model.c
index f46d98b91ee..677713ca29d 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/model/pan_model.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/model/pan_model.c
@@ -90,6 +90,9 @@ const struct pan_model pan_model_list[] = {
                                               MODEL_RATES_X(2, 4, 8,  32,  32, 8)),
    VALHALL_MODEL(PAN_PROD_ID(9, 2, 4), 0, "G68",    "G78", MODEL_ANISO(ALL),  MODEL_TB_SIZES(16384,  8192),
                                               MODEL_RATES_X(2, 4, 8,  32,  32, 8)),
+   /* G710 (kbase TODX, 0xa862): same Valhall v10 core as G610, 7-16 cores. */
+   VALHALL_MODEL(PAN_PROD_ID(10, 8, 2), 0, "G710",   "G710", MODEL_ANISO(ALL),  MODEL_TB_SIZES(32768, 16384),
+                                              MODEL_RATES_X(4, 8, 16,  64,  64, 16)),
    VALHALL_MODEL(PAN_PROD_ID(10, 8, 7), 0, "G610",   "G710", MODEL_ANISO(ALL),  MODEL_TB_SIZES(32768, 16384),
                                               MODEL_RATES_X(4, 8, 16,  64,  64, 16)),
    /* var/cvt/sfu rates might not be correct (we haven't found any detailed documentation) */
